{
  "AC": "A test reproduces the 2026-08-06 d56d incident (driver moves the cursor via add-subtodo/insert while a worker session holds an item): work-item-done from the worker fails loudly with the item id and mover identity instead of silently binding to the wrong item. Lease paths tested: non-owner cursor mutation refused with holder named; expired-lease takeover; --force; owner write refreshes expire; work-item-add and Body/tag edits remain free for non-owners. Multi-record commands (add-subtodo, merge-subtodo, wait-and-merge) are atomic on BOTH store backends (crash between parent and child writes leaves a consistent store). work-item-read's next hint carries item id + rev so the standard poll loop is CAS-protected with no agent behavior change. The todos SKILL.md is updated to document the flags, lease semantics, and the incident as motivation.",
